// Java binding tests (FFM / Panama, JDK 22+).
//
// The binding classes themselves come from java/.build.ae — the same node the
// kotlin/scala/clojure/groovy layers dep, so the JVM family all compile
// against one set of classes rather than five private copies.
//
// Deliberately NOT java.junit: ConformanceTest is a plain `main` runner with
// no JUnit dependency, so the suite needs nothing but a JDK and cannot fail
// on artifact resolution. `java.junit` globs for *Test.class and drives the
// JUnit console launcher, which would mean vendoring junit + hamcrest jars to
// run twelve assertions we already express in ~300 lines. The class is
// written so wrapping the checks in @Test is mechanical if that changes.
// java/pom.xml exists for downstream consumers who do want Maven.
//
// So: javac_test (SDK) for the compile, and a hand-rolled `java` for the run.
//
// The RUN step is the one thing here that cannot be an SDK builder yet.
// lib/java exposes exactly two run builders — `junit` and `junit5` — and both
// glob for *Test.class and drive the JUnit console launcher. There is no
// "run this main class on the test classpath" builder, even though lib/kotlin
// has precisely that (`kotlin_test(ctx, test_class)`, module.ae:561) and
// lib/clojure has `run_main`. Filed as aeb/asks/java-run-main-builder.md.
//
// Consequence: this leaf reconstructs the test classpath by hand, which is
// duplicated knowledge of where javac_test writes (target/test-classes).
import build
import std.os
import java
import java (source_layout)

aeb(cap) {
    b = build.start()
    build.dep(b, "core/.build.ae")
    build.dep(b, "java/.build.ae")
    lib = build.dep_artifact(b, "core/.build.ae", "shared_lib")
    classes = build.dep_artifact(b, "java/.build.ae", "jvm_classpath_deps_including_transitive")
    root = build._get(b, "root")

    java.javac_test(b) {
        source_layout("maven idiomatic")
    }

    // Native.java resolves the engine from $HTMLSANITIZER_LIB. FFM is final
    // in JDK 22 so --enable-preview is NOT needed; the native access flag is,
    // and without it the JVM only warns today but will fail in a future
    // release.
    test_classes = "${root}/target/tests/java/test-classes"
    rc = os.system("cd \"${root}/java\" && HTMLSANITIZER_LIB=\"${lib}\" java --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED -cp \"${classes}:${test_classes}\" org.htmlsanitizer.ConformanceTest")
    if rc != 0 {
        println("java: conformance suite reported failures")
        return 1
    }
    println("java: PASS — 12-check conformance + callback shapes")
    return 0
}
